description:
Learn how to build custom Zoho CRM widgets using HTML, JavaScript, and the Zoho Embedded App SDK to display external UIs directly inside records.

1. Create an extension in Zoho Developer Console and set up a Hosted Widget widget project.
2. Initialize the SDK in your JS file using ZOHO.embeddedApp.init() and fetch record data with ZOHO.CRM.API.getRecord().
3. Deploy the widget and place it directly into a CRM module's Related List or Custom Button.

API / tool used:
- name: Zoho Embedded App SDK
- endpoint: ZOHO.embeddedApp.init() + ZOHO.CRM.API.getRecord()
- scope: ZohoCRM.modules.READ
- docs: Zoho Developer Guide - Widgets

Code (javascript) - Hosted Widget JS file in Zoho Developer Console:
window.onload = function() {
    ZOHO.embeddedApp.on("PageLoad", function(data) {
        if(data && data.EntityId) {
            ZOHO.CRM.API.getRecord({Entity: data.Entity, RecordID: data.EntityId})
            .then(function(response) {
                document.getElementById('recordName').innerText = response.data[0].Last_Name;
            });
        }
    });
    ZOHO.embeddedApp.init();
};

